<Base title="A checkpoint between interpretation and action — TruVector" description="Language models interpret meaning. Coordinates check subject relevance. Arithmetic combines recorded readings and source weights." path="/technology">
<section class="room" style="padding-top:96px"><div class="suite suite--flagship"><p class="kicker">TruVector</p><h1 class="suite-title">A checkpoint between interpretation and action</h1><p class="hero-support" style="margin-top:28px;max-width:66ch">Language models interpret meaning. Coordinates check subject relevance. Arithmetic combines recorded readings and source weights.</p></div></section>
<section class="room" aria-labelledby="section-0"><div class="suite suite--flagship"><h2 class="suite-title" id="section-0">Input and structured readings</h2><p style="margin-top:24px;max-width:70ch">Record the statement, retrieved passages, source assignments, and the authorized instruction and proposed action. Readers return support, refutation, or uncertainty with confidence and a reason. Separate action readings return yes, no, or partly.</p></div></section><section class="room" aria-labelledby="section-1"><div class="suite suite--flagship"><h2 class="suite-title" id="section-1">Numerical aggregation</h2><p style="margin-top:24px;max-width:70ch">Origin-group contributions are divided into per-reply weights, then combined with confidence correction and subject factors. Normalized support S, refutation R, and uncertainty U remain visible. D = S − R measures direction; C measures label concentration rather than calibrated correctness.</p></div></section><section class="room" aria-labelledby="section-2"><div class="suite suite--flagship"><h2 class="suite-title" id="section-2">Reference decision policy</h2><p style="margin-top:24px;max-width:70ch">Fewer than K usable stance readings produces Block with a quorum reason. With quorum, A_no ≥ 0.5 or D ≤ −0.5 with C ≥ 0.5 produces Block. Allow requires D ≥ 0.5, C ≥ 0.5, effective origin weight ≥ 2, reason subject score ≥ 0.6, no unsupported-reader flag, action subject score ≥ 0.7, and A_yes ≥ 0.5. Other outcomes are Review.</p><p style="margin-top:24px;max-width:70ch">The proposed action-input policy additionally requires K usable action readings for Allow. Zero-weight sets with stance quorum route to Review. WP-02 identifies these policy completions and their implementation-conformance requirements.</p></div></section><section class="room" aria-labelledby="section-3"><div class="suite suite--flagship"><h2 class="suite-title" id="section-3">Reconstructable output</h2><p style="margin-top:24px;max-width:70ch">The record contains model and prompt versions, raw readings, source assignments, dependence parameters, weights, S/R/U, D/C, subject scores, action readings, flags, quorum, thresholds, and the decision reasons. It distinguishes substantive opposition from unavailable inputs.</p></div></section><section class="room" aria-labelledby="section-4"><div class="suite suite--flagship"><h2 class="suite-title" id="section-4">Workflow integration</h2><p style="margin-top:24px;max-width:70ch">Retrieval weighting informs passage selection or annotation. Reader aggregation preserves dissent and uncertainty. Action assessment checks instruction consistency alongside application permissions. Origin recovery, delivered context, confidence calibration, and adversarial robustness are evaluated separately.</p></div></section>
<section class="room"><div class="suite suite--flagship"><div class="actions"><a class="btn btn--primary" href="/publications">Read the research papers</a><a class="btn btn--secondary" href="/investors#request">Discuss a solution</a></div></div></section>
</Base>
